# Palomar Comparator safety

- Read `docs/PALOMAR_STYLE.md` before changing compared declarations.
- Read `docs/PALOMAR_EDITORIAL_AUDIT.md` before submission packaging changes.
- Pin explicit universe arity and make unstable instance paths explicit.
- `definition_names` is empty. The holes are the two theorem `sorry`s in
  `Challenge.lean`. Comparator still walks every concrete definition reachable
  from a compared theorem and requires those values to match Solution, even
  when the child is not listed in `comparator.json`.
- Keep `arxiv.md` on the same statements as `Challenge.lean`. The reviewer
  reads the paper with the code. Name `QLambda.Palomar.quotation_capstone`
  for typing and compile reflection, and
  `Quotation.quotation_capstone` for the library theorem that also has CQ
  equality. Do not cite a declaration the repository does not contain.
- Every material symbol in a compared theorem type must be defined without
  `sorry` in `Challenge.lean`.
- Keep `formalization.yaml` aligned with `comparator.json` (`main_results`,
  scope, limitations, sources) and with the Lean pin in `lean-toolchain`.
- Challenge may contain proof holes; Solution and `QLambda/**/*.lean` may not.
- **CI / routine edits:** `bash scripts/palomar_preflight.sh --mechanical-only`
- **Before Palomar submission:** full `bash scripts/palomar_preflight.sh`
  (mechanical + editorial LLM audit). Do not claim readiness unless mechanical
  preflight passes; treat editorial `neutral` synthesis as the submission bar.
